    q: "What is the difference between UTC and GMT?",
    a: "GMT (Greenwich Mean Time) is an astronomical solar time standard based on Earth's rotation at the prime meridian. UTC (Coordinated Universal Time) is the atomic time reference standard maintained by atomic clocks. For general scheduling, both have an identical UTC+0 offset, but UTC is the standard used by modern operating systems and network protocols. Read our comprehensive <a href='/gmt-vs-utc/'>GMT vs UTC guide</a>."
  },
