<section id="business-overlap" class="reveal" aria-label="GMT to EST Business Hour and Forex Overlaps">
  <h2>GMT to EST Business Hour and Forex Overlaps</h2>
  <p>
    Coordinating schedules across global offices requires understanding when standard working hours intersect. For a standard 9:00 AM to 5:00 PM business day, London and major Eastern Time cities share a consistent <strong>3-hour collaborative window</strong> year-round:
  </p>
  <ul style="margin: 16px 0; padding-left: 1.5rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.7;">
    <li><strong>Winter (Standard Time)</strong>: London operates on GMT (UTC+0) and New York operates on EST (UTC-5). The overlap occurs from <strong>2:00 PM to 5:00 PM GMT</strong>, corresponding to <strong>9:00 AM to 12:00 PM EST</strong> (3 hours).</li>
    <li><strong>Summer (Daylight Saving Time)</strong>: London operates on BST (UTC+1) and New York operates on EDT (UTC-4). Because both locations shift forward by one hour, the standard difference remains 5 hours, producing the identical 3-hour overlap: <strong>2:00 PM to 5:00 PM BST</strong>, corresponding to <strong>9:00 AM to 12:00 PM EDT</strong> (3 hours).</li>
  </ul>
